.TH "ANX" "1" "Oct 2026" "anx v1.0.0-339-gbc2b3e8" "Anx User Manual"

.SH NAME
anx-cleanup - Safely detect and prune orphaned, deprecated, and archived components


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanx cleanup [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Detect and safely remove components that are no longer maintained, declared in active manifests,
or have been archived.

.PP
Tracks historical environment memory across:
  1. Orphaned packages and configs tracked in state.json but removed from manifests or active profile.
  2. Deprecated tools and packages recommended for safe purging.
  3. Legacy archived components (e.g. tmux, wdiff, litecli) with lingering host filesystem paths.

.PP
Use --dry-run to preview removals without touching the host filesystem or state.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--archives-only\fP[=false]
	Only prune decommissioned archive remnants from filesystem

.PP
\fB--deprecated-only\fP[=false]
	Only prune deprecated components

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for cleanup

.PP
\fB--orphans-only\fP[=false]
	Only prune orphaned packages tracked in state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Preview actions without mutating the system

.PP
\fB--format\fP="text"
	Output format (text|json|yaml)

.PP
\fB-i\fP, \fB--interactive\fP[=false]
	Force interactive prompts

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable ANSI color rendering

.PP
\fB--offline\fP[=false]
	Disable network queries

.PP
\fB--profile\fP="developer"
	Target profile name

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--theme\fP="tokyo-night"
	UI theme (see 'anx theme list')

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	Verbose execution logging

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Automatically answer yes to confirmations


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Preview all cleanup candidates without removing anything
  anx cleanup --dry-run

  # Interactively review and remove stale components
  anx cleanup

  # Automatically confirm and prune all orphaned components
  anx cleanup --yes --orphans-only
.EE


